{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789300937,"nonce":"05FNcpbMTFsnvtafMaAVLODGKH0=","title":"LLVM tier reads the custom-equality flag from the object, not its class","message":"The inline identity path for == and != on a non-Num operand tests CLASS_FLAG_EQ; the LLVM backend loaded the byte at object+32 (for an instance, the low byte of its fields pointer) instead of class+32, so a class defining == was compared by identity whenever that byte's low bit was clear. Cranelift read the class. Reproducer: tests/e2e.rs e2e_top_tier_equality_honours_a_custom_operator.","files":null}]}